{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c4d5","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0aea4-a602-7083-bf0e-7964935feca1"},"sequence":197,"recorded_at":1780531400000389,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"bc9a7f38-db06-4e74-8937-112c51b35a5b","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.output","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"task_lifecycle","command_id":"bc9a7f38-db06-4e74-8937-112c51b35a5b","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"bc9a7f38-db06-4e74-8937-112c51b35a5b"},"task_stream":{"kind":"task","id":"01a0aea5-248d-7820-91d2-4ccc5ba2850d"},"task_id":"01a0aea5-248d-7820-91d2-4ccc5ba2850d","event":{"kind":"output","task_id":"01a0aea5-248d-7820-91d2-4ccc5ba2850d","chunk":"{\n  \"chunk_id\": \"exec-5-1\",\n  \"command\": \"task-board q 'get(TASK-260830-2zvo8m) { id status checklist }' 2>&1 | python3 -c \\\"import sys,json; d=json.load(sys.stdin); print(json.dumps(d, indent=2)[:8000])\\\"\\necho ===\\ntask-board resource get --help 2>&1 | head -n 40\",\n  \"description\": \"Fetch checklist and resource get help\",\n  \"exit_code\": 0,\n  \"terminal_status\": \"completed\",\n  \"output\": \"{\\n  \\\"checklist\\\": [\\n    {\\n      \\\"text\\\": \\\"Production entry points implement the scoped deliverable: Run provider-specific discover/read/resume/identity checks and refuse unsupported tuple claims\\\",\\n      \\\"done\\\": true\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"text\\\": \\\"Relevant positive, negative, compatibility, and recovery tests pass with logs attached\\\",\\n      \\\"done\\\": true\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"text\\\": \\\"README/doctor/capability evidence and specification traceability are updated without unsupported claims\\\",\\n      \\\"done\\\": true\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"text\\\": \\\"Code written per task description and AC\\\",\\n      \\\"done\\\": true\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"text\\\": \\\"Relevant tests written for new or changed behavior and passing\\\",\\n      \\\"done\\\": true\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"text\\\": \\\"In a managed Story worktree the candidate is left UNCOMMITTED in the worktree for the handoff to snapshot \\\\u2014 never commit on the Story branch. A producer commit moves the branch tip off the recorded checkpoint and the handoff refuses with change_request_candidate_committed_past_checkpoint; repair with `git reset --soft <checkpoint_oid>` before completing again.\\\",\\n      \\\"done\\\": true\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"text\\\": \\\"Every command, message, state, or refusal named in the AC is driven through the production entry point by a named committed test, or is declared a stated bound. Report coverage as a ratio \\\\u2014 `n of m AC rows driven` \\\\u2014 and name the production call site for each. Prose in place of the ratio is not evidence.\\\",\\n      \\\"done\\\": true\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"text\\\": \\\"Gating, refusing, validating, authorizing, or attesting behavior covered by negative tests that fail when the gate admits what it must reject, with the production call site named\\\",\\n      \\\"done\\\": true\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"text\\\": \\\"Every gate ships at least one NARROWING mutant \\\\u2014 the gate stays present and is weakened to admit exactly one member of the class it must reject, and a named test must fail. A delete-only mutant proves only that the gate exists and is not accepted as evidence.\\\",\\n      \\\"done\\\": true\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"text\\\": \\\"A gate that inspects source text is additionally attacked by a mutant that PRESERVES the searched-for token and changes behavior, and the mutant harness executes the behavioral suite, not only the static checker.\\\",\\n      \\\"done\\\": true\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"text\\\": \\\"Lint clean\\\",\\n      \\\"done\\\": true\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"text\\\": \\\"Relevant build/validation commands run after changes and build not broken\\\",\\n      \\\"done\\\": true\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"text\\\": \\\"New outcome artifact attached on the board with a task-scoped name when the work produces notes, logs, screenshots, or other deliverables\\\",\\n      \\\"done\\\": true\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"text\\\": \\\"Important findings, decisions, anomalies, or regressions recorded in logbook when relevant\\\",\\n      \\\"done\\\": true\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"text\\\": \\\"Implementation matches AC\\\",\\n      \\\"done\\\": true\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"text\\\": \\\"Solution fits project architecture\\\",\\n      \\\"done\\\": true\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"text\\\": \\\"Tests green\\\",\\n      \\\"done\\\": true\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"text\\\": \\\"Gate, refusal, validation, authorization, and attestation behavior attacked, not read \\\\u2014 positive-path-only evidence is not accepted\\\",\\n      \\\"done\\\": true\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"text\\\": \\\"If review does not accept the work \\\\u2014 verdict evidence added and status routed by the explicit verdict branches\\\",\\n      \\\"done\\\": true\\n    }\\n  ],\\n  \\\"id\\\": \\\"TASK-260830-2zvo8m\\\",\\n  \\\"status\\\": \\\"reviewing\\\"\\n}\\n===\\nDownload a board resource and save it locally.\\n\\nIf --output is omitted, the file is materialized under:\\n  .temp/resources/<ELEMENT-ID>/<NAME>\\n\\nNested resource names preserve their directory hierarchy below the element.\\n\\nUse --output - to write the resource bytes to stdout.\\n\\nUsage:\\n  task-board resource get <ELEMENT-ID> <NAME> [flags]\\n\\nFlags:\\n  -h, --help            help for get\\n  -o, --output string   Write resource to this path (default: .temp/resources/<ELEMENT-ID>/<NAME>, use - for stdout)\\n\\nGlobal Flags:\\n      --board-dir string         Path to the board directory (overrides TASK_BOARD_DIR and config local.board_dir) (default \\\".task-board\\\")\\n      --context-profile string   Agent context profile override: full or lite\\n      --insecure                 Skip TLS certificate verification (for self-signed certs)\\n      --json                     Output in JSON format\\n      --no-update-check          Disable automatic update check\\n      --remote string            Remote board server URL (overrides TASK_BOARD_REMOTE)\\n      --remote-board string      Remote board ID (overrides TASK_BOARD_ID)\\n\",\n  \"original_output_bytes\": 4544,\n  \"original_output_tokens\": 1136,\n  \"truncated\": false\n}","final_result":true}}}
