{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c6eb","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0aea4-a602-7083-bf0e-7964935feca1"},"sequence":464,"recorded_at":1780531400000923,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"bc9a7f38-db06-4e74-8937-112c51b35a5b","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.output","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"task_lifecycle","command_id":"bc9a7f38-db06-4e74-8937-112c51b35a5b","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"bc9a7f38-db06-4e74-8937-112c51b35a5b"},"task_stream":{"kind":"task","id":"01a0aea5-cb4e-78e0-a9d6-a42f95465f31"},"task_id":"01a0aea5-cb4e-78e0-a9d6-a42f95465f31","event":{"kind":"output","task_id":"01a0aea5-cb4e-78e0-a9d6-a42f95465f31","chunk":"Read text file `.temp/resources/TASK-260830-2zvo8m/TASK-260830-2zvo8m_results-rev2.md`.\n1|# TASK-260830-2zvo8m rev2 results — CR1 rework (P1-1, P1-2 trunk restorations)\n2|\n3|Rework run after the CR1 changes-requested verdict\n4|(`TASK-260830-2zvo8m_review-verdict-rev1.md`, RUN-260917-3ff440).\n5|Product code was fully verified at rev1; rev2 changes **only**\n6|`LOGBOOK.md` and `README.md`, restoring two trunk hunks the base\n7|refresh had carried stale pre-trunk copies over. No product-code\n8|change; no new behavior; rev1 test/mutant/traceability evidence\n9|stands and every gate below re-ran green on the rev2 tree.\n10|\n11|Story tip unchanged: `54ed1b3` on trunk `e4e3e88`. Candidate left\n12|UNCOMMITTED in `.temp/STORY-260830-315721/worktree`.\n13|\n14|## What changed since rev1\n15|\n16|### P1-1 — LOGBOOK.md: 3lt2xv trunk entry restored\n17|\n18|Re-inserted the 5-line block from `git show HEAD:LOGBOOK.md`\n19|(lines 8–12) between the 2zvo8m entry and the 3uzfyn entry.\n20|Newest-first order preserved: 2zvo8m, 3lt2xv, 3uzfyn, kp4zpu, ….\n21|\n22|Restored hunk (byte-identical to HEAD, verified by script):\n23|\n24|```text\n25|### TASK-260917-3lt2xv — release-agnostic cataloggen check via -adopted\n26|- CONTRACT: validation command 21 was pinned to explicit v0.6.0 inputs, …\n27|- GATE: command 21 is now `go run ./internal/catalog/cmd/cataloggen -adopted -output internal/catalog/catalog_gen.go -check`; …\n28|- TESTS: adopted positives, byte-identity …, narrowing mutants …, harmless control SURVIVED. …\n29|- DOCS: README regenerate block and tool row document the `-adopted` form and the explicit equivalent. …\n30|```\n31|\n32|(`…` abbreviates here only; the file carries the full HEAD lines.)\n33|`git diff HEAD -- LOGBOOK.md` is now purely additive: 51 insertions,\n34|0 deletions.\n35|\n36|### P1-2 — README.md: both `-adopted` hunks restored\n37|\n38|1. Regenerate block — restored the `-adopted` check line, the\n39|   derivation paragraph, and the explicit-equivalent block, keeping\n40|   the Native-resume smoke section and figure updates:\n41|\n42|```bash\n43|go generate ./internal/catalog\n44|go run ./internal/catalog/cmd/cataloggen -adopted -output internal/catalog/catalog_gen.go -check\n45|go test ./internal/catalog ./internal/cataloggen ./internal/catalog/cmd/cataloggen -count=1\n46|```\n47|\n48|```text\n49|The `-adopted` form derives the metadata and lock inputs from the code-level\n50|adopted release, so the check stays valid when the adopted release changes.\n51|The explicit equivalent pins the same inputs by path:\n52|```\n53|\n54|```bash\n55|go run ./internal/catalog/cmd/cataloggen -metadata internal/catalog/catalog.v0.6.0.json -contracts internal/specpin/v0.6.0.lock.json -output internal/catalog/catalog_gen.go -check\n56|```\n57|\n58|2. Go-toolchain table row — restored the `-adopted` command with the\n59|   explicit-selector note:\n60|\n61|```text\n62|`go run ./internal/catalog/cmd/cataloggen -adopted -output internal/catalog/catalog_gen.go -check` (`-metadata`/`-contracts` select the same inputs explicitly);\n63|```\n64|\n65|Both restored segments verified byte-identical to HEAD (regen\n66|section, tool row, and LOGBOOK block compared as slices: all True;\n67|`-adopted` count 3 = 3; `TASK-260917-3lt2xv` count 1 = 1).\n68|\n69|`git diff HEAD -- README.md`: 79 insertions, 13 deletions. Every\n70|deleted line is an intentional traceability-figure rewrite for this\n71|leaf (113 cases, 29/463 clauses, full=2 partial=4 sliver=3,\n72|unevidenced 48→44, admitted bindings 1→2 with the Section 2.4\n73|sentences) — none touches cataloggen/`-adopted` content. Full list\n74|in `rev2-readme-deleted-lines.txt` inside the evidence tarball.\n75|\n76|Restoration method: targeted insertion of exact HEAD bytes via a\n77|throwaway script (`/tmp/restore_trunk_hunks.py`, kept in the\n78|tarball); neither file was wholesale-checked-out.\n79|\n80|## Stale-copy audit (trunk 62d4463 → e4e3e88 vs candidate)\n81|\n82|Trunk changed (non-board paths): `LOGBOOK.md`, `README.md`,\n83|`internal/catalog/catalog.go`, `internal/catalog/catalog_test.go`,\n84|`internal/catalog/cmd/cataloggen/main.go`,\n85|`internal/catalog/cmd/cataloggen/main_test.go`,\n86|`task-board.config.json`.\n87|\n88|- Candidate tracked modifications: `LOGBOOK.md`, `README.md`\n89|  (both fixed above), `internal/provhost/identity.go`,\n90|  `internal/provhost/probe.go`,\n91|  `internal/traceability/cmd/tracecheck/main_test.go`,\n92|  `internal/traceability/ownership.v0.6.0.json`,\n93|  `internal/traceability/traceability.go`,\n94|  `internal/traceability/traceability_test.go` — the\n95|  provhost/traceability paths are disjoint from the trunk list, so\n96|  they cannot revert trunk content.\n97|- `git diff HEAD --name-only -- internal/catalog\n98|  task-board.config.json` → empty (0 paths); `task-board.config.json`\n99|  shows no diff.\n100|- Untracked candidate paths (`internal/provhost/accessors_test.go`,\n101|  `internal/resumesmoke/`) are new files; they revert nothing.\n102|- `.task-board/` paths in the trunk range are board artifacts, not\n103|  worktree scope; the candidate touches none.\n104|\n105|## Validation (all observed this session on the rev2 tree)\n106|\n107|26-command suite = the 18 README Go-toolchain commands plus 8 CI\n108|extras; every command exit 0 (fuzz legs additionally require the\n109|`^fuzz: elapsed` execution proof):\n110|\n111|| # | Command | Result |\n112|| - | ------- | ------ |\n113|| 1 | `go run ./internal/traceability/cmd/tracecheck` | exit 0 — 113 cases, 29/463 |\n114|| 2 | `tracecheck -section 6.2` | exit 0 (admitted) |\n115|| 3–5 | `go test ./internal/config ./internal/localstore ./internal/scalar -cover -count=1` | exit 0 (via ./... legs) |\n116|| 6 | scalar fuzz `FuzzScalarProductionEntries` 100x | elapsed ✓ |\n117|| 7–9 | `go test ./internal/canonicaljson ./internal/axerror ./internal/cliresult -cover -count=1` | exit 0 (via ./... legs) |\n118|| 10–13 | canonicaljson 4 fuzz targets 100x | elapsed ✓ each |\n119|| 14 | `go generate ./internal/catalog` + `git diff --exit-code` on `catalog_gen.go` | clean |\n120|| 15 | `cataloggen -adopted -output internal/catalog/catalog_gen.go -check` | exit 0 |\n121|| 16 | `go test ./... -v -count=1` | exit 0 — 28 ok, 0 FAIL, 1 top-level SKIP (`TestDumpSweepSites`, skips by design when `AX_SWEEP_DUMP` is unset; canonicaljson harness hook outside candidate scope) |\n122|| 17 | `go test ./... -cover -count=1` | exit 0 — 28 coverage lines, resumesmoke 77.0% |\n123|| 18 | `go build ./...` | exit 0 |\n124|| 19 | `gofmt -l internal` | clean (empty) |\n125|| 20 | `go vet ./...` | exit 0 |\n126|| 21 | `GOOS=windows go vet ./...` | exit 0 |\n127|| 22 | `GOOS=linux go build ./...` | exit 0 |\n128|| 23 | `GOOS=windows go build ./...` | exit 0 |\n129|| 24 | JSON validity over `git ls-files '*.json'` | pass |\n130|| 25 | `git diff --check` | clean |\n131|| 26 | `go test -race ./internal/resumesmoke ./internal/provhost ./internal/sessprofile` | exit 0 |\n132|\n133|Beyond the 26, also green this session:\n134|\n135|- Focused `go test ./internal/resumesmoke ./internal/provhost\n136|  ./internal/sessprofile ./internal/traceability/... -count=1` —\n137|  exit 0 (41.4 s / 8.8 s / 5.8 s / 2.9 s / 48.5 s).\n138|- `go test ./... -count=1` (non-verbose) — exit 0, 28 ok, 0 FAIL.\n139|- cigate contract gates (6 tests) — exit 0.\n140|- cigate README-claim gates incl.\n141|  `TestRealREADMECarriesNoPositiveClaim` (all probes unavailable)\n142|  — exit 0, so the restored README carries no positive capability\n143|  claim.\n144|- `tracecheck -section 2.4` — exit 0 (admitted).\n145|- secconftest fuzz targets (5 of the 13 total; 13/13 with elapsed\n146|  lines, target list derived from `-list`, count pin 13 holds).\n147|- Native-Windows bind rows skip loudly with the exact reason\n148|  (`windows native-store bind requires a Windows host; cell … is\n149|  pinned by TestResumeMatrixCoversEverySpecRow`).\n150|\n151|## Coverage and hygiene\n152|\n153|- AC coverage: 16 of 16 rows driven through production entries —\n154|  reviewer-confirmed at rev1; rev2 touches no production code, and\n155|  the focused + full suites re-ran green on the rev2 tree.\n156|- `git status` shows only candidate paths (8 modified + 2 untracked\n157|  entries); no `__pycache__`, no `.pyc`; candidate UNCOMMITTED; no\n158|  commit made on the Story branch.\n159|- Conformance matrix unchanged from rev1; re-attached under the\n160|  rev2 name per the rework brief.\n161|\n162|## Attached\n163|\n164|- `TASK-260830-2zvo8m_results-rev2.md` (this file)\n165|- `TASK-260830-2zvo8m_conformance-matrix-rev2.md`\n166|- `TASK-260830-2zvo8m_producer-evidence-rev2.tar.gz` (real gzip:\n167|  rev2 validation logs, diffs, restoration script, byte-identity\n168|  proof)","final_result":true}}}
