, content preserved\" —\n24|that claim is false for this entry.\n25|\n26|Repair: re-insert the 3lt2xv block from\n27|`git show HEAD:LOGBOOK.md` between the new `2zvo8m` entry and the\n28|`3uzfyn` entry (newest-first order).\n29|\n30|### P1-2 — README `-adopted` docs deleted\n31|\n32|The leaf removed trunk's 3lt2xv README docs in two places, both present\n33|in `HEAD` and the trunk base, absent in the worktree:\n34|\n35|1. Regenerate block: `cataloggen -adopted -output\n36|   internal/catalog/catalog_gen.go -check` plus the paragraph \"The\n37|   `-adopted` form derives the metadata and lock inputs …\", replaced by\n38|   the explicit `-metadata`/`-contracts` form only.\n39|2. Validation toolchain table row: the `-adopted … (-metadata/-contracts\n40|   select the same inputs explicitly)` command replaced by the explicit form.\n41|\n42|`-adopted` is live production behavior (`run()` in\n43|`internal/catalog/cmd/cataloggen`, covered by `main_test.go`\n44|`TestRunAdopted*`); both forms exit 0 on this tree (observed). The\n45|validated command 21 is the `-adopted` form, which the README no longer\n46|documents.\n47|\n48|Repair: restore both `-adopted` hunks from `git show HEAD:README.md`.\n49|\n50|No P2. No Stop-The-Line (rework is autonomous, no external decision needed).\n51|\n52|## What was verified green (own instruments, live tree read-only)\n53|\n54|- Whole-Story delta: 55 paths trunk→candidate confirmed; worktree tracked\n55|  files equal candidate (`git diff --quiet f6bde3c --` excluding the 15\n56|  new-file paths that are untracked-in-worktree/tracked-in-candidate:\n57|  exit 0); leaf paths beyond checkpoints exactly the 23 stated paths;\n58|  `task-board.config.json` byte-identical to trunk and HEAD;\n59|  checkpoints `a6dfaf2`, `54ed1b3` signatures Good (oparin@me.com).\n60|- `go test ./internal/resumesmoke/ -count=1`: exit 0 (26.2 s full suite,\n61|  includes shipped mutant harness + real-kill test).\n62|- `go test ./internal/provhost/ ./internal/sessprofile/ -count=1`: exit 0.\n63|- `go test ./internal/sessprofile/ ./internal/traceability/... -count=1`:\n64|  exit 0 (tracecheck suite 70.5 s).\n65|- Shipped `TestSmokeMutantsAreKilled`: green twice (full suite + focused\n66|  rerun, 23.2 s): 10 narrowing mutants KILLED, harmless control SURVIVED.\n67|- Own narrowing mutants (private /tmp module copies, checkout never\n68|  written; raw log `review-mutants-raw.log`):\n69|  m1 matrix admits gemini-wsl2 C as A → KILLED by\n70|  `TestSmokeRowVerdicts/gemini-0.54.4-wsl2-amd64` (rc=1);\n71|  m2b record digest admits gated verdict → KILLED by\n72|  `TestSmokeTamperedRecordRefuses` (rc=1);\n73|  m3 confidence admits strong for codex → KILLED by\n74|  `TestSmokeStrongConfidenceFails` (rc=1);\n75|  m4 profile vocabulary admits turbo → KILLED by\n76|  `TestSmokeParamsRefusals/bad_profile` (rc=1);\n77|  c0 harmless comment control → SURVIVED as expected.\n78|  (One rejected probe design disclosed: m2 digest-prefix-compare\n79|  SURVIVED because single-bit flips avalanche SHA-256; superseded by m2b.)\n80|- Spec-derivation sensitivity: flipping `Codex / macOS | A / C / C` to\n81|  `C / C / C` in a private doc copy reddens\n82|  `TestResumeMatrixCoversEverySpecRow` (FAIL observed).\n83|- 27 Section 8.4 rows confirmed in `SPEC.v0.6.0.md` table; cell mapping\n84|  independently matched provider by provider (codex A×4, claude A×3+C,\n85|  gemini A/macOS+linux/windows C/wsl2, muse pin + C×3 + ?, antigravity\n86|  C×4, pi A+C×3, qwen U, future ?); WSL2/Windows never collapse\n87|  (`platformCell` keeps all four platforms distinct).\n88|- Zero-call refusals: qwen×8, future-plugin×8, not-a-provider×8 subtests\n89|  plus `TestSmokeMuseOnePatchOffPinRefuses` all PASS; refused shape\n90|  asserts exactly one check (`resume-cell=pass`), no digests, nil calls,\n91|  and the fake has no handler scripted so any call would fatal.\n92|- Promotion attacks: `TestSmokePromotionAttemptRefuses` (flipped +\n93|  resigned), `TestSmokeInconsistentFailRefuses`,\n94|  `TestSmokeWhitespaceVariantRefuses` PASS in suite.\n95|- Closed shape / no capability: `TestSmokeRecordCarriesNoCapabilityClaim`\n96|  (16 members, no capab/doctor/enabled) PASS; canary asserted on every\n97|  row; real-process run byte-identical (`TestSmokeThroughRealProviderProcess`) PASS.\n98|- Durability: `TestStoreRealKillBetweenWriteAndSync` PASS 3× (suite + 2\n99|  focused reruns); `TestStoreDisagreementQuarantines`,\n100|  `TestStoreReplayIsIdentical`, crash-hook tests PASS in suite.\n101|- Provhost accessors: `ProbeBuild`/`SplitIdentifyResult` consume\n102|  `decodeValidated*` members only (read `probe.go`/`identity.go` diff);\n103|  zero own refusal sites confirmed; `accessors_test.go` PASS in suite.\n104|- Traceability: `tracecheck` exit 0, `113 cases, 29/463 clauses`\n105|  (matches pinned test figures); 12 added acceptance cases enumerated\n106|  (`resumesmoke-matrix/run/record/store`, `provhost-resume-tuple-gate`,\n107|  plus 7 predecessor cases); all 12 clause excerpts for 2.4/5.5/7.7/8\n108|  found in the pinned doc (whitespace-normalized); all 8 production\n109|  declarations exist; self-minted binding probe refused by tracecheck.\n110|- Hygiene: `gofmt -l internal` clean; `go vet` (incl. `GOOS=windows`\n111|  on resumesmoke+provhost) exit 0; `-race` on focused smoke tests exit 0;\n112|  `cataloggen -adopted -check` and explicit form both exit 0;\n113|  native-Windows rows skip loudly\n114|  (`windows native-store bind requires a Windows host; cell \"A\" is pinned\n115|  by TestResumeMatrixCoversEverySpecRow`); no `__pycache__`/`.pyc`;\n116|  `git status` shows only the 23 candidate paths; candidate UNCOMMITTED.\n117|\n118|## Coverage ratio\n119|\n120|16 of 16 producer AC rows driven through production entries — confirmed\n121|by the green suites above (row verdicts, probe/identify/bind/quiescence/\n122|resume negatives, Appendix B gates, durability, tamper/consistency).\n123|Story-close: ownership bindings 2.4 full 4/4, 5.5 sliver 1/3, 7.7 partial\n124|3/4, 8 sliver 4/12 with honest gaps — accepted; LOGBOOK/README\n125|preservation — FAILED (P1-1, P1-2).\n126|\n127|## Refusal-census observations (not blockers)\n128|\n129|- `smoke.go:158` tuple-gate-fail arm has no dedicated test reaching it\n130|  (matrix/gate agreement covers derived tuples; any matrix-admit vs\n131|  gate-refuse divergence would need an off-matrix version probe).\n132|- Transport-failure arms (`unframeable`/`call failed` in probe/identify/\n133|  resume) are covered by construction (params validation + strict fake),\n134|  not by dedicated failing-call tests.\n135|- `deriveVerdict` unexpected-skip→fail arm is exercised only via\n136|  C-cell gated paths, not as a standalone skip violation.\n137|\n138|## Rework scope for producer\n139|\n140|Restore the two hunks (P1-1, P1-2), re-run `go test\n141|./internal/resumesmoke ./internal/provhost ./internal/sessprofile\n142|./internal/traceability/... -count=1`, re-verify `git status` shows only\n143|candidate paths, republish rev2. No product-code change required.","final_result":true}}}
