ed positives, byte-identity …, narrowing mutants …, harmless control SURVIVED. …\n29|- DOCS: README regenerate block and tool row document the `-adopted` form and the explicit equivalent. …\n30|```\n31|\n32|(`…` abbreviates here only; the file carries the full HEAD lines.)\n33|`git diff HEAD -- LOGBOOK.md` is now purely additive: 51 insertions,\n34|0 deletions.\n35|\n36|### P1-2 — README.md: both `-adopted` hunks restored\n37|\n38|1. Regenerate block — restored the `-adopted` check line, the\n39|   derivation paragraph, and the explicit-equivalent block, keeping\n40|   the Native-resume smoke section and figure updates:\n41|\n42|```bash\n43|go generate ./internal/catalog\n44|go run ./internal/catalog/cmd/cataloggen -adopted -output internal/catalog/catalog_gen.go -check\n45|go test ./internal/catalog ./internal/cataloggen ./internal/catalog/cmd/cataloggen -count=1\n46|```\n47|\n48|```text\n49|The `-adopted` form derives the metadata and lock inputs from the code-level\n50|adopted release, so the check stays valid when the adopted release changes.\n51|The explicit equivalent pins the same inputs by path:\n52|```\n53|\n54|```bash\n55|go run ./internal/catalog/cmd/cataloggen -metadata internal/catalog/catalog.v0.6.0.json -contracts internal/specpin/v0.6.0.lock.json -output internal/catalog/catalog_gen.go -check\n56|```\n57|\n58|2. Go-toolchain table row — restored the `-adopted` command with the\n59|   explicit-selector note:\n60|\n61|```text\n62|`go run ./internal/catalog/cmd/cataloggen -adopted -output internal/catalog/catalog_gen.go -check` (`-metadata`/`-contracts` select the same inputs explicitly);\n63|```\n64|\n65|Both restored segments verified byte-identical to HEAD (regen\n66|section, tool row, and LOGBOOK block compared as slices: all True;\n67|`-adopted` count 3 = 3; `TASK-260917-3lt2xv` count 1 = 1).\n68|\n69|`git diff HEAD -- README.md`: 79 insertions, 13 deletions. Every\n70|deleted line is an intentional traceability-figure rewrite for this\n71|leaf (11