{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c877","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0aea4-a602-7083-bf0e-7964935feca1"},"sequence":662,"recorded_at":1780531400001319,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"bc9a7f38-db06-4e74-8937-112c51b35a5b","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.output","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"task_lifecycle","command_id":"bc9a7f38-db06-4e74-8937-112c51b35a5b","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"bc9a7f38-db06-4e74-8937-112c51b35a5b"},"task_stream":{"kind":"task","id":"01a0aea6-63bb-7791-9718-b3aef0c2b0ce"},"task_id":"01a0aea6-63bb-7791-9718-b3aef0c2b0ce","event":{"kind":"output","task_id":"01a0aea6-63bb-7791-9718-b3aef0c2b0ce","chunk":"{\n  \"chunk_id\": \"exec-21-1\",\n  \"command\": \"head -n 70 LOGBOOK.md | cat -n | head -n 70\\necho === base head ===\\ngit show e4e3e8834675cf3814effd3b2673b4931dfbf311:LOGBOOK.md | head -n 20 | cat -n | head -n 20\",\n  \"description\": \"Check LOGBOOK newest-first order\",\n  \"exit_code\": 0,\n  \"terminal_status\": \"completed\",\n  \"output\": \"     1\\t# Flight Logbook\\n     2\\t\\n     3\\t> Institutional memory. Concise, factual, high-signal.\\n     4\\t> Newest entries first. One block per insight.\\n     5\\t\\n     6\\t## 2026-09-17\\n     7\\t\\n     8\\t### TASK-260830-2zvo8m — native-resume smoke framework (story-final leaf)\\n     9\\t\\n    10\\t- PRODUCTION: new `internal/resumesmoke` (`Run` drives probe,\\n    11\\t  identify-session, discovery-bind, quiescence-precondition, and\\n    12\\t  resume-plan through `provhost.Host.Call`; `ResumeCell` reads the\\n    13\\t  Section 8.4 native-resume direction with Appendix B version gates;\\n    14\\t  `VerifyRecord` enforces the closed smoke record, omit-self digest,\\n    15\\t  and verdict consistency; `Store`/`Load` install content-addressed,\\n    16\\t  no-replace, fsynced evidence) plus two zero-refusal-site provhost\\n    17\\t  replay accessors (`ProbeBuild`, `SplitIdentifyResult`) that consume\\n    18\\t  validated members, never the body.\\n    19\\t- REFUSAL DIRECTION: U/? tuples refuse before any adapter call; C\\n    20\\t  tuples gather read-only evidence and gate the resume plan with the\\n    21\\t  Section 19.3 citation; only A cells pass. No smoke API promotes a\\n    22\\t  gated cell, and passing smoke advertises no capability (no\\n    23\\t  capability map, no doctor surface; Section 8.3 stays the only\\n    24\\t  authority). Muse off-pin reads unknown (Appendix B unsettled),\\n    25\\t  matching the landed tuple gate.\\n    26\\t- MUTANTS: committed `TestSmokeMutantsAreKilled` kills 10/10\\n    27\\t  narrowing mutants (resume gate, probe drift, confidence, bind,\\n    28\\t  digest scope, consistency, disagreement length, quiescence,\\n    29\\t  mapping, matrix) with the harmless comment control SURVIVED. Each\\n    30\\t  mutant runs in a private module copy: the first harness patched\\n    31\\t  the checkout in place and raced parallel tree-walking censuses\\n    32\\t  (`specdoc` read a half-written file under `go test ./...`), so\\n    33\\t  the shipped harness never writes the checkout.\\n    34\\t- DEFECTS FOUND BY TESTS (fixed): record verification carried two\\n    35\\t  equivalent integrity checks (canonical reconstruction subsumed the\\n    36\\t  omit-self digest compare, which could never fire independently) -\\n    37\\t  dropped reconstruction, kept the owner-idiom digest compare; crash\\n    38\\t  test scanned a 19-char prefix of a 20-char filename and missed the\\n    39\\t  killed install.\\n    40\\t- IDEMPOTENCY/CRASH: identical inputs replay byte-identical records;\\n    41\\t  identical Store retries reuse the path; disagreeing bytes refuse\\n    42\\t  for quarantine; real-kill test (`SIGKILL` between write and fsync\\n    43\\t  via re-executed helper) recovers byte-identical evidence.\\n    44\\t- TRACEABILITY (story-close): bindings for 2.4 (full 4/4), 5.5\\n    45\\t  (sliver 1/3), 7.7 (partial 3/4), 8 (sliver 4/12) with 12 new\\n    46\\t  acceptance cases; `tracecheck` now 113 cases, 29/463 clauses;\\n    47\\t  `-section 2.4` admitted alongside 6.2; README figures and pin\\n    48\\t  tests updated deliberately.\\n    49\\t- BOUNDS (stated): native-Windows bind rows need a Windows host\\n    50\\t  (host separator vs platform-native proof rule) and skip loudly on\\n    51\\t  POSIX with cells still pinned by derivation; quiescence consumed\\n    52\\t  as valid-and-safe only (proof-to-tuple binding belongs to the\\n    53\\t  quiescence owner); record integrity detects tampering, not a\\n    54\\t  digest-plus-checklist forgery (local evidence, no adversary).\\n    55\\t- COVERAGE: 16 of 16 AC rows driven through production entries;\\n    56\\t  results, conformance matrix, and producer evidence tarball\\n    57\\t  attached to the task; candidate left uncommitted.\\n    58\\t\\n    59\\t### TASK-260917-3lt2xv — release-agnostic cataloggen check via -adopted\\n    60\\t- CONTRACT: validation command 21 was pinned to explicit v0.6.0 inputs, so a Story re-pointing the catalog at a new revision failed construction at its own gate. The fix declares the adopted release once (`catalog.Adopted`, consumed by `Current()`) and adds a cataloggen `-adopted` mode deriving `internal/catalog/catalog.<adopted>.json` and `internal/specpin/<adopted>.lock.json` relative to `-root` (default \\\".\\\"). Mixed `-adopted` with explicit `-metadata`/`-contracts`, a missing derived input (message names the derived path), and a lock whose source release differs from adopted are refused before generation; otherwise the same Generate call and `-check`/`-output` semantics run byte-identically to the explicit form.\\n    61\\t- GATE: command 21 is now `go run ./internal/catalog/cmd/cataloggen -adopted -output internal/catalog/catalog_gen.go -check`; every other validation command unchanged. No catalog content, metadata, lock, or generated-output change.\\n    62\\t- TESTS: adopted positives, byte-identity (adopted vs explicit v0.6.0 vs committed), and all refusals driven through the production `run` entry; the configured-command test asserts the `-adopted` shape and runs it rooted at the repo. Narrowing mutants per refusal plus a byte-identity derivation mutant, all killed; harmless control SURVIVED. Both the candidate `-adopted` command and trunk's explicit command are green on the tree.\\n    63\\t- DOCS: README regenerate block and tool row document the `-adopted` form and the explicit equivalent. No behavior or availability claims added.\\n    64\\t### TASK-260830-3uzfyn — profile resolution, set-profile, and provider mapping\\n    65\\t- PRODUCTION: new `internal/sessprofile` (Section 2.4 derivation over\\n    66\\t  the session head and the checkpoint event-head closure, `Projector`\\n    67\\t  over the sessrepo entries, pure `MintChangeEvent`, `Transactor`\\n    68\\t  set-profile with replay-on-retry, reducer-level pair\\n    69\\t  projections/checks, `ResolveCreationProfile`) plus provhost\\n    70\\t  `ResolveMapping`/`ProjectLaunchArgv` and the seventh refusal\\n=== base head ===\\n     1\\t# Flight Logbook\\n     2\\t\\n     3\\t> Institutional memory. Concise, factual, high-signal.\\n     4\\t> Newest entries first. One block per insight.\\n     5\\t\\n     6\\t## 2026-09-17\\n     7\\t\\n     8\\t### TASK-260917-3lt2xv — release-agnostic cataloggen check via -adopted\\n     9\\t- CONTRACT: validation command 21 was pinned to explicit v0.6.0 inputs, so a Story re-pointing the catalog at a new revision failed construction at its own gate. The fix declares the adopted release once (`catalog.Adopted`, consumed by `Current()`) and adds a cataloggen `-adopted` mode deriving `internal/catalog/catalog.<adopted>.json` and `internal/specpin/<adopted>.lock.json` relative to `-root` (default \\\".\\\"). Mixed `-adopted` with explicit `-metadata`/`-contracts`, a missing derived input (message names the derived path), and a lock whose source release differs from adopted are refused before generation; otherwise the same Generate call and `-check`/`-output` semantics run byte-identically to the explicit form.\\n    10\\t- GATE: command 21 is now `go run ./internal/catalog/cmd/cataloggen -adopted -output internal/catalog/catalog_gen.go -check`; every other validation command unchanged. No catalog content, metadata, lock, or generated-output change.\\n    11\\t- TESTS: adopted positives, byte-identity (adopted vs explicit v0.6.0 vs committed), and all refusals driven through the production `run` entry; the configured-command test asserts the `-adopted` shape and runs it rooted at the repo. Narrowing mutants per refusal plus a byte-identity derivation mutant, all killed; harmless control SURVIVED. Both the candidate `-adopted` command and trunk's explicit command are green on the tree.\\n    12\\t- DOCS: README regenerate block and tool row document the `-adopted` form and the explicit equivalent. No behavior or availability claims added.\\n    13\\t\\n    14\\t### TASK-260830-21gygk — rev16 rework: normalize Go aliases in the sealed-capability census\\n    15\\t- REVIEW FINDING CLOSED (CR15 P2-A): the package-wide `go/types` census\\n    16\\t  compared lexical `*types.TypeName` objects, so a Go alias could bypass the\\n    17\\t  sealed `checkpointSeal`/`checkpointSealToken` inventory. The initial alias\\n    18\\t  baseline admitted the direct, token, chained, and container plants; its\\n    19\\t  recorded exit was 1 before the fix.\\n    20\\t- FIX (`internal/sessquery/rev11_regression_test.go`): every sealed type and\\n\",\n  \"original_output_bytes\": 8169,\n  \"original_output_tokens\": 2043,\n  \"truncated\": false\n}","final_result":true}}}
