%d survived=%d, want %d and 1\", killed, survived, len(smokeMutants)-1)\n160|\t}\n161|}\n162|\n163|// smokeModuleRoot returns the repository root two directories\n164|// above this package: the tree the harness copies mutants from.\n165|func smokeModuleRoot(t *testing.T) string {\n166|\tt.Helper()\n167|\tworking, err := os.Getwd()\n168|\tif err != nil {\n169|\t\tt.Fatalf(\"os.Getwd: %v\", err)\n170|\t}\n171|\treturn filepath.Join(working, \"..\", \"..\")\n172|}\n173|\n174|// copyModuleForMutant copies the module sources a mutant run needs\n175|// — go.mod, go.sum, and the internal tree — into a fresh temp\n176|// directory, applies the mutant there, and returns the copy. The\n177|// checkout is only read, never written.\n178|func copyModuleForMutant(t *testing.T, root string, mutant smokeMutant) string {\n179|\tt.Helper()\n180|\tworkdir := t.TempDir()\n181|\tfor _, name := range []string{\"go.mod\", \"go.sum\"} {\n182|\t\tdata, err := os.ReadFile(filepath.Join(root, name))\n183|\t\tif err != nil {\n184|\t\t\tt.Fatalf(\"read %s: %v\", name, err)\n185|\t\t}\n186|\t\tif err := os.WriteFile(filepath.Join(workdir, name), data, 0o600); err != nil {\n187|\t\t\tt.Fatalf(\"stage %s: %v\", name, err)\n188|\t\t}\n189|\t}\n190|\tcopyDir(t, filepath.Join(root, \"internal\"), filepath.Join(workdir, \"internal\"))\n191|\tpath := filepath.Join(workdir, \"internal\", \"resumesmoke\", mutant.file)\n192|\toriginal, err := os.ReadFile(path)\n193|\tif err != nil {\n194|\t\tt.Fatalf(\"read %s: %v\", mutant.file, err)\n195|\t}\n196|\tif bytes.Count(original, []byte(mutant.find)) != 1 {\n197|\t\tt.Fatalf(\"mutant find occurs %d times in %s, want exactly once\", bytes.Count(original, []byte(mutant.find)), mutant.file)\n198|\t}\n199|\tmutated := bytes.Replace(original, []byte(mutant.find), []byte(mutant.replace), 1)\n200|\tif err := os.WriteFile(path, mutated, 0o600); err != nil {\n201|\t\tt.Fatalf(\"apply mutant: %v\", err)\n202|\t}\n203|\treturn workdir\n204|}\n205|\n206|// copyDir copies one directory tree to a fresh destination,\n207|// preserving file modes. Symlinks refuse: the module tree the\n208|// harness copies carries none, and a link would escape the copy.\n209|func copyDir(t *testing.T, source, destination string) {\n210|\tt.Helper()\n211|\tentries, err := os.ReadDir(source)\n212|\tif err != nil {\n213|\t\tt.Fatalf(\"read %s: %v\", source, err)\n214|\t}\n215|\tif err := os.MkdirAll(destination, 0o755); err != nil {\n216|\t\tt.Fatalf(\"stage %s: %v\", destination, err)\n217|\t}\n218|\tfor _, entry := range entries {\n219|\t\tif entry.Type()&os.ModeSymlink != 0 {\n220|\t\t\tt.Fatalf(\"refusing to copy symlink %s\", filepath.Join(source, entry.Name()))\n221|\t\t}\n222|\t\tfrom := filepath.Join(source, entry.Name())\n223|\t\tto := filepath.Join(destination, entry.Name())\n224|\t\tif entry.IsDir() {\n225|\t\t\tcopyDir(t, from, to)\n226|\t\t\tcontinue\n227|\t\t}\n228|\t\tdata, err := os.ReadFile(from)\n229|\t\tif err != nil {\n230|\t\t\tt.Fatalf(\"read %s: %v\", from, err)\n231|\t\t}\n232|\t\tinfo, err := entry.Info()\n233|\t\tif err != nil {\n234|\t\t\tt.Fatalf(\"stat %s: %v\", from, err)\n235|\t\t}\n236|\t\tif err := os.WriteFile(to, data, info.Mode()); err != nil {\n237|\t\t\tt.Fatalf(\"stage %s: %v\", to, err)\n238|\t\t}\n239|\t}\n240|}","correlation_facts":{"tool_name":"read_file","outcome":"success"}}}
{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000cb65","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0aea4-a602-7083-bf0e-7964935feca1"},"sequence":1037,"recorded_at":1780531400002069,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"bc9a7f38-db06-4e74-8937-112c51b35a5b","payload_type":"tool.result","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"tool_result","command_id":"bc9a7f38-db06-4e74-8937-112c51b35a5b","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"bc9a7f38-db06-4e74-8937-112c51b35a5b"},"call_id":"call_01a0aea8470377cc91e9ab5e3ef7667b","text":"Read text file `internal/resumesmoke/matrix_derive_test.go`.\n1|package resumesmoke\n2|\n3|import (\n4|\t\"strings\"\n5|\t\"testing\"\n6|\n7|\t\"github.com/relux-works/agent-session-manager/internal/provhost\"\n8|\t\"github.com/relux-works/agent-session-manager/internal/specdoc\"\n9|)\n10|\n11|// This file derives the Section 8.4 native-resume expectations from\n12|// the pinned specification text and requires the smoke matrix to\n13|// cover every row exactly. The cell values are never retyped here:\n14|// the test parses the provider/platform rows and the native-resume\n15|// cell out of the document, so a matrix value that drifts from the\n16|// pinned contract reddens here rather than passing against a\n17|// hand-typed copy of the same mistake.\n18|\n19|// specRow is one parsed Section 8.4 row: the provider, the platform,\n20|// the architectures it names, the native-resume cell, and the\n21|// version the row pins when it names one.\n22|type specRow struct {\n23|\tprovider      string\n24|\tplatform      string\n25|\tarchitectures []string\n26|\tcell          Cell\n27|\tpinned        string\n28|}\n29|\n30|// derivedFixtureVersions are the probe versions the row tests run\n31|// with. Versions are fixtures, not derivations — Section 8.4 pins\n32|// only the Muse macOS arm64 probe — except the Muse pin itself,\n33|// which the row text carries.\n34|var derivedFixtureVersions = map[string]string{\n35|\t\"codex\":          \"0.147.0\",\n36|\t\"claude\":         \"2.1.229\",\n37|\t\"gemini\":         \"0.54.4\",\n38|\t\"muse\":           \"0.1.0\",\n39|\t\"antigravity\":    \"1.1.14\",\n40|\t\"pi\":             \"0.73.1\",\n41|\t\"qwen\":           \"1.0.0\",\n42|\t\"future-plugin\":  \"0.0.0\",\n43|\t\"not-a-provider\": \"0.0.0\",\n44|}\n45|\n46|// TestResumeMatrixCoversEverySpecRow derives every Section 8.4 row\n47|// and requires the smoke matrix to read the row's native-resume\n48|// cell for each named tuple. The parsed row count is asserted so a\n49|// parser that silently derives nothing fails closed.\n50|func TestResumeMatrixCoversEverySpecRow(t *testing.T) {\n51|\trows := parseSection84(t)\n52|\tif len(rows) != 27 {\n53|\t\tt.Fatalf(\"parsed %d section 8.4 rows, want 27\", len(rows))\n54|\t}\n55|\tvar tuples []specRow\n56|\tfor _, row := range rows {\n57|\t\ttuples = append(tuples, expandRow(row)...)\n58|\t}\n59|\tfor _, row := range tuples {\n60|\t\trow := row\n61|\t\tfor _, architecture := range row.architectures {\n62|\t\t\tarchitecture := architecture\n63|\t\t\tt.Run(row.provider+\"/\"+row.platform+\"/\"+architecture, func(t *testing.T) {\n64|\t\t\t\tversion := derivedFixtureVersions[row.provider]\n65|\t\t\t\tif row.pinned != \"\" {\n66|\t\t\t\t\tversion = row.pinned\n67|\t\t\t\t}\n68|\t\t\t\tcell, gate := ResumeCell(row.provider, version, row.platform, architecture)\n69|\t\t\t\tif cell != row.cell {\n70|\t\t\t\t\tt.Fatalf(\"ResumeCell(%s %s %s %s) = %q, want row cell %q\", row.provider, version, row.platform, architecture, cell, row.cell)\n71|\t\t\t\t}\n72|\t\t\t\tif gate == \"\" {\n73|\t\t\t\t\tt.Fatal(\"ResumeCell returned an empty gate citation\")\n74|\t\t\t\t}\n75|\t\t\t\tif row.pinned != \"\" {\n76|\t\t\t\t\t// A pinned row accepts only its probe: one\n77|\t\t\t\t\t// patch off the pin is unknown, per the\n78|\t\t\t\t\t// Appendix B unsettled-behavior rule the\n79|\t\t\t\t\t// matrix cites. The pin itself comes from\n80|\t\t\t\t\t// the row text; the off-pin version below\n81|\t\t\t\t\t// is the derivation's probe of it.\n82|\t\t\t\t\toff := offPinVersion(row.pinned)\n83|\t\t\t\t\toffCell, _ := ResumeCell(row.provider, off, row.platform, architecture)\n84|\t\t\t\t\tif offCell != CellUnknown {\n85|\t\t\t\t\t\tt.Fatalf(\"ResumeCell(%s %s %s %s) = %q, want unknown off the %s pin\", row.provider, off, row.platform, architecture, offCell, row.pinned)\n86|\t\t\t\t\t}\n87|\t\t\t\t}\n88|\t\t\t})\n89|\t\t}\n90|\t}\n91|}\n92|\n93|// TestResumeMatrixAgreesWithTupleGate requires the matrix and the\n94|// landed Section 8.4 tuple gate to agree on the direction for every\n95|// derived tuple: available and conditional rows pass the gate, and\n96|// unsupported and unknown rows refuse. Both sides are production;\n97|// the agreement pins them against each other.\n98|func TestResumeMatrixAgreesWithTupleGate(t *testing.T) {\n99|\trows := parseSection84(t)\n100|\tif len(rows) != 27 {\n101|\t\tt.Fatalf(\"parsed %d section 8.4 rows, want 27\", len(rows))\n102|\t}\n103|\tvar tuples []specRow\n104|\tfor _, row := range rows {\n105|\t\ttuples = append(tuples, expandRow(row)...)\n106|\t}\n107|\tfor _, row := range tuples {\n108|\t\tversion := derivedFixtureVersions[row.provider]\n109|\t\tif row.pinned != \"\" {\n110|\t\t\tversion = row.pinned\n111|\t\t}\n112|\t\tfor _, architecture := range row.architectures {\n113|\t\t\ttuple := provhost.BuildTuple{ProviderID: row.provider, ProviderVersion: version, Platform: row.platform, Architecture: architecture}\n114|\t\t\terr := provhost.CheckResumeTuple(tuple)\n115|\t\t\tswitch row.cell {\n116|\t\t\tcase CellAvailable, CellConditional:\n117|\t\t\t\tif err != nil {\n118|\t\t\t\t\tt.Errorf(\"CheckResumeTuple(%+v) = %v, want pass for %q row\", tuple, err, row.cell)\n119|\t\t\t\t}\n120|\t\t\tdefault:\n(more lines below)","correlation_facts":{"tool_name":"read_file","outcome":"success"}}}
