alue test can decide the rest. Clause 5.5#2's destination-derivation MUST belongs to the destination adapter rather than the host record.\\\",\\n3568:          \\\"id\\\": \\\"5.5#3\\\",\\n3606:      \\\"gap\\\": \\\"ForRelease only returns the reviewed typed catalog rows that reference 7.2; the Section 7.2 host envelope (framing, deadlines, size limits, dispatch, and recovery) is implemented in internal/provhost under the Section 7.6 and Section 7.7 bindings, and no clause of Section 7.2 is enumerated against an acceptance case, so the registry makes no clause-level claim about the 7 obligations it carries.\\\"\\n3686:      \\\"gap\\\": \\\"ForRelease only returns the reviewed typed catalog rows that reference 7.5; the host-side Section 7.5 operation conformance (SpawnPlan launch and resume bodies, identify-session results, materialize-status recovery, and the single operation plus operation_id mutation key) is implemented in internal/provhost under the Section 7.6 and Section 7.7 bindings, and no clause of Section 7.5 is enumerated against an acceptance case, so the registry makes no clause-level claim about the 53 obligations it carries.\\\"\\n3736:        \\\"section:7.7\\\"\\n3748:      \\\"gap\\\": \\\"Section 7.7 clause 7.7#2 stays undisclosed: its omit rule is enforced, but its machine-local-alias sentence is only half-decided, because a shell word that expands to unrestricted mode without spelling a table token is beyond argv inspection (shell aliases never expand under execve, owned by secprim). ResolveMapping decides the exact-version probe rule the other three clauses need.\\\",\\n3751:          \\\"id\\\": \\\"7.7#1\\\",\\n3760:          \\\"id\\\": \\\"7.7#3\\\",\\n3768:          \\\"id\\\": \\\"7.7#4\\\",\\n\",\n  \"original_output_bytes\": 2203,\n  \"original_output_tokens\": 551,\n  \"truncated\": false\n}","final_result":true}}}
